\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Through all the changing scenes of life,
\par In trouble and in joy,
\par The praises of my God shall still
\par My heart and tongue employ.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Of His deliverance I will boast,
\par Till all that are distressed
\par From my example comfort take,
\par And charm their griefs to rest.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. O magnify the Love with me,
\par With me exalt His name;
\par When in distress to Him I called,
\par He to my rescue came.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. The hosts of God encamp around 
\par The dwellings of the just;
\par Deliverance He affords to all
\par Who on His succour trust?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. O make but trial of His love;
\par Experience will decide
\par How blest they are, and only they,
\par Who in His truth confide.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. Fear Him, ye saints, and you will then
\par Have nothing else to fear;
\par Make you His service your delight,
\par He'll make your wants His care.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

